        "original_id": "eeeca519-85fa-5c8c-8c30-bcecc4f8e59b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400\n- Companies: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia\n- Topics: NASCAR Cup Series title sponsorship, essay contest naming\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Diageo acquired Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- Crown Royal is a blended Canadian whisky.\n- From 2007 to 2011, Crown Royal, a former title sponsor of the Toyota Owners 400, named the race after the winner of an essay contest held during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two Richmond Raceway NASCAR Cup Series races each year, with the Toyota Owners 400 serving as the spring race first.",
